1,2 $ Spores inamyloid
1,3 $ Spores amyloid

2,0 $ Cheilocystidia and pleurocystidia conspicuous and long pedicelate arising below the hymenium; clamp connections present $ Albomagister
2,0 $ Cheilocystidia present or absent; pleurocystidia rare, if present arising from the hymenium; clamp connections rarely present $ Tricholoma

3,0 $ Spores verrucose $ Leucopaxillus
3,4 $ Spores smooth

4,0 $ Cheilocystidia and pleurocystidia present $ Dennisiomyces
4,5 $ Pleurocystidia absent; cheilocystidia present or absent

5,0 $ Cheilocystidia present, edges of lamellae sterile; distributed in the Southern Hemisphere $ Porpoloma
5,6 $ Cheilocystidia present or absent; distributed in temperate forests and grasslands of the Northern Hemisphere or in the tropics

6,0 $ Basidiocarps not changing color where cut or bruised; lamellae sometimes forked; cheilocystidia present and well differentiated; distributed in the tropics $ Corneriella
6,0 $ Basidiocarps changing red where cut or bruised; lamellae not forked; cheilocystidia absent or poorly differentiated; distributed in temperate forests and grasslands of the Northern Hemisphere $ Pseudotricholoma


